Z-VLA simulation post-training source

This tree is copied from the supplied Z-VLA project without its Git history,
weights, data or runtime outputs. Existing Limx Dynamics Apache-2.0 notices
remain in their source files. The simulation engine includes code shared with
FluxVLA Engine (https://github.com/FluxVLA/FluxVLA), including its registry
and builder utilities. Preserve the Limx Dynamics attribution on those files.
The project maintainer has selected Apache-2.0 for project simulation source
without a separate license notice, including training, data preparation and
benchmark integration code. This decision does not relicense official simulator
source or remove existing third-party licenses and attribution. See
../LICENSE_POLICY.md for the scope.

The training logger and metric modules are independently implemented for this
release under Apache-2.0. `zvla/engines/utils/registry.py` identifies
OpenMMLab as its source under Apache-2.0.

LIBERO/Plus, MetaWorld, RoboTwin and RoboDojo environments are external
dependencies installed separately under their upstream terms. Any source copied
or adapted from those projects must retain its upstream notices and terms.

metaworld_benchmark/prompts.py adapts the official MetaWorld task descriptions:
https://metaworld.farama.org/benchmark/task_descriptions/
Copyright (c) 2019 Meta-World Team. MIT License; the full notice and terms are
included in LICENSES/MetaWorld-MIT.txt. This table retains MIT licensing.

robodojo/xpolicylab_policy/ZVLA/setup_eval_env_client.sh and
setup_eval_policy_server.sh adapt the XPolicyLab demo_policy and DP launch
templates at revision 72b3a52f2b069220088ef824ade5890885858379:
https://github.com/XPolicyLab/XPolicyLab
The upstream templates are Apache-2.0; that license text is included in
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

The optional fa2_custom_mask extension is retained. Its project bindings,
launchers and mask integration use Apache-2.0; the modified FlashAttention
Hopper headers and CUTLASS/C++ CuTe headers retain BSD-3-Clause licensing and
their original copyright notices. The source, AUTHORS, license texts and
fa2_custom_mask/NOTICE are included in the wheel and source distribution.
See fa2_custom_mask/NOTICE for the pinned upstream sources and modifications.
